---
description: "Cursor-only adapter for cross-repo contract validation"
alwaysApply: false
---

Cursor-only adapter. Use when an API, DTO, transport edge, or cross-repo boundary is in scope.

## Pipeline

1. Read the owner contract and the consuming repo route.
2. Verify endpoints, callers, DTOs, literals, and flags in current source.
3. Use graph or index tooling only as support and only with explicit repo targeting plus freshness proof.
4. Confirm the boundary with focused tests or the existing repo gate.

Do not broaden a local fix into a new transport edge or silent contract change.
